              "sub_category": "Instantaneous Speed & Instantaneous Velocity",
              "chapter": "Motion in a Straight Line",
              "exam_name": "NEET 2016 · NCERT",
              "question": "<p>If the velocity of a particle is <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(v=At+Bt^{2},\\)</span> where <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(A\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(B\\)</span> are constants, then the distance travelled by it between <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(1~\\text{s}\\)</span>&nbsp;and <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(2~\\text{s}\\)</span>&nbsp;is:</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\"><tbody><tr><td>1.</td><td><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(3A+7B\\)</span></td><td>2.</td><td><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{3}{2}A+\\frac{7}{3}B\\)</span></td></tr><tr><td>3.</td><td><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{A}{2}+\\frac{B}{3}\\)</span></td><td>4.</td><td><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{3A}{2}+4B\\)</span></td></tr></tbody></table>",
